      <td>28.1%</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>aarch64-linux</td>
      <td>2517</td>
      <td>27.6%</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>x86_64-darwin</td>
      <td>2008</td>
      <td>22.0%</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>aarch64-darwin</td>
      <td>2007</td>
      <td>22.0%</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Total</strong></td>
      <td><strong>9087</strong></td>
      <td><strong>100%</strong></td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

**total package/architecture combinations:** **9087**



when changing the nix implementation of `buildRustPackage`, like when updating `rustc`/`cargo` or the toolchain, this can multiply the rebuild workload across the architectures.

